-- title:
--   Spherical Whittaker Hecke eigenfunctions on GL₃ come from principal series
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a height one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, let $\psi_v$ be an additive character of the completion $\mathbb Q_v$ with values in $\mathbb C$, let $\alpha : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to \mathbb C$ satisfy $\|\alpha_i\| = 1$ for all $i$, and let $W : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v) \to \mathbb C$. Assume: $W$ is right invariant under `localMaximalCompact3`, the subgroup of matrices $k$ all of whose entries, and all of whose entries of $k^{-1}$, have valuation $\le 1$, in the sense that $W(gu) = W(g)$ for all $g$ and all such $u$; $W$ is a coset eigenfunction for the generator $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,1,1)$ with eigenvalue $N(v)\,(\alpha_0+\alpha_1+\alpha_2)$ and for the generator $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\varpi,1)$ with eigenvalue $N(v)\,(\alpha_0\alpha_1+\alpha_0\alpha_2+\alpha_1\alpha_2)$, where $\varpi$ is the chosen uniformiser, $N(v)$ the absolute norm of $v$, and being a coset eigenfunction with eigenvalue $\lambda$ means that for every finite family of representatives $(\mathrm{reps}_i)$ satisfying [`HeckeIntegralSeam.IsHeckeCosetSystem`](def/LocalLanglands_HeckeCosetSystem.html#L15) for the compact subgroup and the given generator one has $\sum_i W(g\,\mathrm{reps}_i) = \lambda\,W(g)$ for all $g$; $W(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\varpi,\varpi)\,g) = \alpha_0\alpha_1\alpha_2\,W(g)$ for all $g$; $W(n(x,y,z)g) = \psi_v(x+y)W(g)$ for all $x,y,z \in \mathbb Q_v$ and all $g$, where $n(x,y,z)$ is the upper triangular unipotent matrix with entries $x,y,z$; the level `addCharLevel` of $\psi_v$, the supremum of the set of $n \in \mathbb Z$ with $\psi_v$ trivial on $\{v(x) \le \exp n\}$, is $0$; and $\psi_v \neq 1$. Then there is a triple $\chi : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to \mathrm{Hom}(\mathbb Q_v^\times, \mathbb C^\times)$ of group homomorphisms, each locally constant, each of modulus one at every argument, and each trivial on every unit $x$ with $\|x\| = 1$, together with a $\mathbb C$-linear functional $\Lambda$ on the space `principalSeries3` $v\,\chi$ of locally constant functions $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$ that are invariant under left translation by the upper unipotent matrices and satisfy $f(a g) = \mathrm{torusChar3}(\chi)(a)\,\mathrm{halfModulus3}(a)\,f(g)$ for diagonal $a$, such that $\Lambda$ is a $\psi_v$-Whittaker functional, i.e. $\Lambda$ applied to the right translate of $F$ by $n(x,y,z)$ equals $\psi_v(x+y)\,\Lambda(F)$, and an element $f$ of that space with $W =$ `coefficientFn` $\Lambda\,f$, that is $W(g) = \Lambda(f(\,\cdot\,g))$ for all $g$.
--
--   This is the local spherical identification at a finite place in the Langlands–Tunnell argument: a $K_v$-invariant $\psi_v$-Whittaker function which is an eigenfunction of the two spherical Hecke generators and of the centre, with unimodular Satake parameters, is realised as a Whittaker coefficient of an unramified unitary principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$. The triple $\chi$ is produced existentially, so no normalisation of the Satake dictionary $\chi_i(\varpi) \leftrightarrow \alpha_i$ is exported; the statement feeds the results on the cyclic subspace generated by such a $W$.
